{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Note that the series has terms that alternate in sign, has **even** factorials in the denominator, and has even powers of $~\\pi~$ in the numerator. This suggests that we work with the Maclaurin series for $~\\cos x\\,$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Recall that\n\n$\\displaystyle\\cos x=1-\\frac{{{x}^{2}}}{2!}+\\frac{{{x}^{4}}}{4!}-...+{{\\left( -1 \\right)}^{n}}\\frac{{{x}^{2n}}}{\\left( 2n \\right)!}+...$\n\nIt follows that\n\n$\\displaystyle3\\cos (x^2)=3-\\frac{3{{x}^{4}}}{2!}+\\frac{3{{x}^{8}}}{4!}-...+{3{\\left( -1 \\right)}^{n}}\\frac{{{x}^{4n}}}{\\left( 2n \\right)!}+...$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Hence, the given series converges to $~3\\cos ( \\pi^2  )\\,$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Evaluate the Maclaurin series.**\n\n$3-\\dfrac{{{3\\pi }^{4}}}{2!}+\\dfrac{{3{\\pi }^{8}}}{4!}-...+{{3\\left( -1 \\right)}^{n}}\\dfrac{{{\\pi }^{4n}}}{\\left( 2n \\right)!}+...$\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$3$","correct":false},{"content":"$-3$","correct":false},{"content":"$3\\cos ( \\pi^2  )$","correct":true},{"content":"$-3\\cos ( \\pi^2  )$","correct":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
